 "about": "ROUGH WATERS (Code/Game/Voyage/RoughWaters.cs; the user, 9 Oct 2026: 'an intelligent realistic current and weather system that can blow and push the ship off course and rough ocean areas'). Real places where the sea is worse than the wind alone makes it. kind: 'race' (a tide race: rough while the stream runs, worst with the wind against it, quiet at slack water), 'bar' (the bar of a river mouth: rough with the wind blowing on to it; 'open_to' is the compass bearing it lies open to), 'shoal' (sands and banks: broken water in any fresh wind), 'cape' (a headland with no shelter: rough in a fresh wind, worse while the tide runs). lat, lon: degrees. reach_km: how near she must be to be in it. rough: how bad it is at its worst (1: a man bailing and the hull working as in a gale; 2: twice that). find: the thing of discoveries_793.json that is the same place: she knows its name when she has found that. 'today' is the place's name now, for whoever edits this file: the game never shows it. EVERY NUMBER IS A STARTING GUESS TO TUNE. Bake/world/check_rough_waters.py checks every place against the world bake, the lanes and the tide model.",
